WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Cheap flights and Instagram made the world's fragile wonders accessible to millions, and then

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.080
the crowds began to erode what they came to see.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.780
This is Unintended Consequences, episode 79.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.760
In the summer of 2018, tie authorities closed Maya Bay.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:22.280
The small cove on Kofi Filae had drawn more than 5,000 visitors a day after appearing

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.180
in the 2000 film The Beach.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.220
Coral had been trampled, water was clouded by sunscreen and boat fuel.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.700
The once white sand had compacted into hard pan.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.840
Officials had not set out to damage the bay.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.200
They had welcomed the tourism that arrived after the movie as a straightforward economic

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.680
gain for southern Thailand.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:48.180
The closure lasted four years because the daily volume had crossed the threshold at which

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:53.240
the physical process is maintaining the bay could no longer keep pace with the rate of disturbance.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.780
After the Second World War, governments and airlines worked to make long distance travel

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.480
available beyond the wealthy.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.920
Jet aircraft introduced in the late 1950s lowered costs per passenger.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:13.300
D-regulation in the United States in 1978 and in Europe in the 1990s allowed new low-cost

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.720
carriers to enter the market.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.160
Ryanair began operations in 1985, an easy jet in 1995.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.140
They offered fairs that sometimes fell below the price of a train ticket between the same cities.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:32.340
Social media platforms after 2010 let travelers share precise locations with followers.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.960
This turned once obscure waterfalls in Iceland or temples in Peru into recognizable destinations.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.980
Policy makers and industry leaders viewed these developments as extensions of earlier public

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.580
health and leisure policies.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:52.680
Wider access to nature and culture would improve lives and spread economic benefits to host

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:58.580
communities. The assumption was that more visitors would simply scale the existing benefits without

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:04.980
changing the underlying resource. Budget carriers expanded routes rapidly through the 2000s.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.400
By 2019, European low-cost flights exceeded 1.2 billion seats annually.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.480
Cruise lines increased capacity with vessels carrying more than 4,000 passengers docking

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.300
at Venice's Historic Center several times a week.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:28.140
Instagram's location tagging feature rolled out in 2010 made it simple for users to mark exact

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:35.760
coordinates. By 2017, posts tagged at Iceland's Celgelands Foss waterfall had risen into the hundreds

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:42.420
of thousands. Local governments initially celebrated the revenue. Maya Bay saw visitor numbers climbed

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:49.440
from a few hundred a day in the 1990s to over 5,000 after the film. Venice's tourism office

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:55.660
promoted day trips as a way to spread spending. Early data showed hotel occupancy and restaurant

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:02.440
receipts rising. The same mechanisms that increased access removed any practical limit on daily volume.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:09.340
In Venice, day trippers reached an estimated 20-25 million annually by the mid-2000s.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:16.440
The resident population fell below 50,000. Housing converted to short-term rentals raised rents

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.160
beyond the reach of many local families. Wastewater systems designed for a smaller permanent

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:28.720
population overflowed during peak summer days. The wakes of large cruise ships accelerated erosion

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.940
along the Lagoon's foundations. At Machu Picchu, daily visitors climbed past 5,000.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.820
This compacted soil on the Inka trails and increased landslide risk during rainy seasons.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:47.840
In Iceland, roadside pullouts at popular sites were widened repeatedly. Parking still overflowed

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.020
onto fragile moss and search-and-rescue calls rose with the number of unprepared hikers.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:58.800
Maya Bay's coral covered declined by roughly 80% in the decade after the film,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.340
according to surveys by Thailand's Department of National Parks. The causal chain was straight

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:10.700
forward. Zero or near-zero marginal cost for each additional visitor, combined with visible

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:16.240
social proof on social media, produced daily loads that exceeded the ecological and

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:22.180
infrastructural thresholds of the sites. An increase from a few hundred visitors to 5,000

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:28.340
represents roughly a 10-fold to 20-fold rise in daily foot traffic, boat moorings, and chemical

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:34.180
inputs. All of this was concentrated on a cove whose coral and sediment systems had evolved

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:40.660
under far lower disturbance rates. Residents left historic centers removing the very local life

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:46.040
that many tourists had hoped to encounter. Emergency closures then shifted pressure to

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.960
neighboring sites that lacked even basic management plans. Revenue accrued to short-term

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:58.040
operators and platforms while the costs of erosion control, rescue services, and habitat repair

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:05.320
remained with public agencies and the remaining residents. Thailand closed Maya Bay in June 2018

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:14.160
for four years. It reopened in 2022 with a daily cap of 375 visitors and a requirement that

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:20.500
boats more offshore. Venice introduced a five-year-old day trip or fee for peak periods beginning

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:27.500
in 2024, paired with a reservation system. Enforcement remains limited to a few entry points.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:33.420
Iceland has added parking fees and timed entry at several highland sites and has funded

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:39.480
trail hardening with a portion of the revenue. Peru now requires advanced tickets for Machu Picchu

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:45.760
and has caped daily entries near 4000. These measures have reduced peak loads at the most

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:52.920
stressed locations. Yet they have also concentrated demand on still open alternatives and created administrative

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:58.920
costs that smaller municipalities struggle to meet. Some residents note that the fees generate

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:04.260
revenue without restoring the quieter character of the places before mass visitation began.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:10.940
Shared scenic or cultural resources without effective gatekeeping tend toward overuse because

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:16.840
the cost of each additional visitor falls almost entirely on the resource itself rather than on

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:22.300
the visitor or the platform that directs them there. Pricing, quotas, and physical limits can

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:27.860
restore balance, but only when they are set below the visible degradation threshold and are

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:33.880
forced consistently. The pattern appears again with any open access, digital, or physical

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:40.400
commons whose popularity grows faster than its carrying capacity. How might current platforms and

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:46.220
transport systems be designed so that the next wave of newly accessible places does not repeat the

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:52.360
same sequence? That's the case for today. The lessons tend to travel further when you share them,

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.060
so send this one to someone who'd find it useful and subscribe wherever you're listening.

